## APPENDIX I: GLOSSARY OF TECHNICAL TERMS & ACRONYMS

| Term/Acronym | Definition |
|--------------|------------|
| **ABM** | Agent-Based Modeling: Computational simulation of autonomous agents interacting within an environment to study emergent system behavior. |
| **CEGAR** | Counterexample-Guided Abstraction Refinement: Formal verification technique that iteratively refines abstract models using counterexamples from model checking. |
| **CPM** | Cost Per Million tokens: Standard metric for comparing inference pricing across models and providers. |
| **DTMDP** | Discrete-Time Markov Decision Process: Stochastic modeling framework for sequential decision-making under uncertainty. |
| **Edge-Hybrid** | Infrastructure topology combining centralized data centers with distributed edge nodes to balance latency, energy, and scalability. |
| **LTL** | Linear Temporal Logic: Formal specification language for expressing safety and liveness properties over time. |
| **PCTL** | Probabilistic Computation Tree Logic: Extension of CTL for specifying probabilistic properties of stochastic systems. |
| **PUE** | Power Usage Effectiveness: Ratio of total facility power to IT equipment power; lower values indicate higher efficiency. |
| **RAG** | Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Architecture that enhances LLM responses by retrieving relevant external knowledge before generation. |
| **SIO Framework** | Sovereign Inference & Orchestration Framework: Layered model of AI sovereignty across Data, Compute, Orchestration, and Regulatory dimensions. |
| **VCR** | Value Capture Ratio: Economic metric comparing domestic inference value retention vs. foreign API dependency. |
| **WUE** | Water Usage Effectiveness: Liters of water consumed per kWh of IT energy; critical metric for arid-region data centers. |

